\ A `parameter{ }` default body is in neither the freezer's word list nor its
\ quotation list: freeze seeds its callees into the worklist without recording
\ the body itself. The call inside it still has to count against the callee.
\
\ `scale-it` is called twice with different types -- a fixnum here, a float
\ inside the default -- so nothing about its parameter is provable. Missing the
\ default's call site would prove `fixnum` from the visible site alone, and
\ codegen would then unbox the float payload as an integer.
\
\ Build-only. Evaluating the default at runtime reports `unknown-word` in a
\ default AOT build, a separate pre-existing gap in what a parameter default's
\ callee gets serialized into. `make aot-param-inference-check` asserts what
\ this file is here for, which is that the freeze proves nothing about
\ `scale-it`.

scale-it: ( x -- y ) [ 2 * ] ;
thing: parameter{ [ 1.5 scale-it ] } ;

5 scale-it .
thing get .
